WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 1.5 · Strategic Foundations
Organisational form and identity

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Choose the form that fits how your work will be funded and governed, not the most credible one.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Your organisational form is the legal and economic vehicle for your mission. It decides who controls it, what happens to any surplus, how it can raise money and what it must report.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
The main families of form

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:38.981
Informal group: No separate legal entity; members agree among themselves and may be personally liable. For example: Three neighbours run a tool library for a year to test the idea.

6
00:00:38.981 --> 00:00:50.681
Nonprofit or foundation: Members or a board control it; any surplus stays in, never paid to owners. For example: A youth club registers as an association so it can apply for grants.

7
00:00:50.681 --> 00:01:02.381
Social purpose company: Shareholders own it; profits can be paid out unless its rules limit this. For example: A bakery that trains young people funds itself through sales and a small loan.

8
00:01:02.381 --> 00:01:17.504
Cooperative or hybrid: Members own a cooperative, one vote each; a hybrid pairs a nonprofit with a trading company. For example: Growers run a shop as a cooperative; or a nonprofit owns a café that funds its work.

9
00:01:17.904 --> 00:01:18.504
Why it matters

10
00:01:18.504 --> 00:01:24.548
1. It decides who governs, what happens to surplus and who regulates you.

11
00:01:24.548 --> 00:01:30.593
2. It shapes how you can raise money: grants, sales, loans or investment.

12
00:01:30.593 --> 00:01:36.896
3. Changing form later is possible but costs time and money.

13
00:01:37.296 --> 00:01:37.896
What it guides

14
00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:43.570
1. How you set up governance and accountability in the Organise course.

15
00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.763
2. How you manage money and raise funds.

16
00:01:47.763 --> 00:01:53.326
3. Registration and your legal duties in Module 10.

17
00:01:53.726 --> 00:01:54.326
What to avoid

18
00:01:54.326 --> 00:02:00.370
Choosing the form that sounds most credible, not the one that fits.

19
00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:06.044
Registering before testing the idea, when informal would do for now.

20
00:02:06.044 --> 00:02:13.089
Skipping local advice from someone with a legal background or an accountant.

21
00:02:13.689 --> 00:02:15.489
You write a comparison of forms and your current preference.

22
00:02:15.489 --> 00:02:19.489
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:20.989 --> 00:02:24.089
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
